    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0517" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Strobel.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 47.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received Mr. Palmer’s No. 35 of the
                    16th ultimo, reporting that, in compliance with my No. 37 of November 25, last,
                    he had addressed notes to the Spanish Government in regard to the indemnity
                    claimed by the Rev. Mr. Doane for his imprisonment and to the threatened seizure
                    of the lands of his mission by the governor of Ponape.</p>
                <p>His action is approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
